<pre><h1>   Exercise Name: Seated Incline Dumbbell Hammer Curl</h1></pre>
<u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>
This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates Seated Incline Dumbbell Hammer Curls. The video highlights both the biceps (Biceps Brachii) and the forearm muscles (Brachialis and Brachioradialis) in bright glowing colors, showing how leaning back on an inclined bench targets the muscles while maintaining a neutral grip (palms facing inward).
 Exercise Name: Seated Incline Dumbbell Hammer Curl
 Target Muscles: Brachialis, Brachioradialis (forearms), and Biceps (Biceps Brachii)
 Secondary Muscles: Wrist Extensors & Flexors

</div>
</div>
<pre>
<h1>
    
    How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1> <u><h4><b>1. Setup</b></h4></u>
 Set an adjustable workout bench to an incline angle of roughly 45 to 60 degrees. Sit back against the pad with your feet flat on the floor, holding a dumbbell in each hand with a neutral grip (palms facing each other). Let your arms hang straight down naturally.
 <u><h4><b>2. Curling Phase</b></h4></u>
 Keep your back pressed against the seat pad and upper arms stationary. Exhale as you curl both dumbbells upward toward your shoulders, maintaining your neutral grip throughout the entire movement.
 <u><h4><b>3. Peak Squeeze</b></h4></u>
 Pause briefly at the top position to squeeze your brachialis and forearm muscles tightly.
 <u><h4><b>4. Lowering Phase</b></h4></u>
 Inhale as you lower the dumbbells back down under full control until your arms are fully extended at your sides.



<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Greater Muscle Stretch:</b> Sitting at an incline places the biceps and forearms under a deeper stretch at the bottom position, leading to better muscle hypertrophy.
 <b>◉Eliminates Cheating:</b> Having your back supported against the incline bench prevents you from using torso momentum or swinging your back to lift the weights.
 <b>◉Arm & Forearm Thickness:</b> Combines the thickness-building benefits of the hammer grip with the stretch-focused stimulus of an incline position.



<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep your head and back firmly against the bench pad throughout each rep—do not lift your chest or neck forward as you lift the dumbbells.
